    "notes": "The permanent exterior of the Arctic and Antarctic Museum in the former St. Nicholas Edinoverie Church in Saint Petersburg, in its circa-2008 museum configuration. Includes the mapped four projecting fronts, the principal Marata approach, two-tier classical massing and green central dome. The separate chapels, interiors and temporary restoration works are outside this model. The footprint and entrance are mapped. The roof, the four fronts and the upper section are interpretive estimates from the cleared dome view and written descriptions."
